course: dictionary
lesson: 7201
title: Petting animals safely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Petting means stroking an animal gently and kindly. Read the words around it for clues. «At the petting farm you hold a chick gently in cupped hands» tells you that petting is slow, soft and careful.
explain: Petting can also be a place. A «petting zoo» is where children can touch and stroke farm animals. The word is used in the phrase «petting the dog» and in the name of the place, so check the sentence to see which meaning is used.
explain: Before petting a dog, ask the owner. Let it sniff your hand first, stroke gently along its back, and stop if it moves away or growls. An animal that moves away is telling you it does not want to be petted right now.
fact: Petting means stroking an animal gently and kindly.
fact: A petting zoo is a place where children can touch and stroke farm animals.
fact: Wash your hands with soap and water after petting animals.
fact: Animals can carry germs such as E. coli on their fur and in their droppings, without being ill themselves.
fact: Some children who did not wash their hands properly after visiting a petting farm became very ill and had to go to hospital.
exercise: What does petting mean? | Feeding animals at night | Cleaning out a stable with a brush | *Stroking an animal gently and kindly | Chasing animals around a field
exercise: What is a petting zoo? | *A place where children can touch and stroke farm animals | A big cage for lions | A shop that sells pet food | A school for vets
exercise: Before petting a dog, what should you do first? | Shout loudly to wake it up | *Ask the owner | Give it a big hug from behind | Pull its tail to get its attention
test: Why should you wash your hands after petting animals? | Your hands will smell nice | To make your hands warm | *To remove germs such as E. coli | To stop your nails growing
test: After a dog has sniffed your hand, how should you stroke it? | Upside down on its tummy | Quickly across its nose | *Gently along its back | Hard against its fur
exam: Why should you not eat in the petting area? | Petting zoos only sell drinks | *Animals can carry germs like E. coli on their fur and in their droppings | The animals might be jealous | Food gets too cold there
